{
  "_doc": "Parameter layouts, darktable 5.6, little-endian, every field 4 bytes (f float, i int or enum). A field counts as confirmed in the CI KPIs only if `test` names an integration test that passes in the same run. Human-checked fields without a test keep `test: null`. `default` is the value darktable gives a new instance (from dt_iop_*_params_t in src/iop/*.c); it is what xmp.default_params() writes, and a module with a field lacking one has no default_params (toneequal enums, channelmixerrgb). Every layout is also checked against the blobs of darktable's built-in presets by tests/test_darktable.py::test_preset_*.",
  "crop": {
    "version": 3, "size": 24,
    "fields": [
      {"name": "left", "type": "f", "test": "tests/test_darktable.py::test_crop_edges_are_normalized"},
      {"name": "top", "type": "f", "test": "tests/test_darktable.py::test_crop_edges_are_normalized"},
      {"name": "right", "type": "f", "test": "tests/test_darktable.py::test_crop_edges_are_normalized"},
      {"name": "bottom", "type": "f", "test": "tests/test_darktable.py::test_crop_edges_are_normalized"},
      {"name": "ratio_n", "type": "i", "test": "tests/test_darktable.py::test_crop_ratio_trims_to_the_ratio",
       "note": "short side of the aspect (4 for 4:5, 2 for 3:2). 0 with |ratio_d| = 1 is original image, 0/0 is freehand. An export trims the crop to a multiple of the ratio on each side; the GUI keeps the lock"},
      {"name": "ratio_d", "type": "i", "test": "tests/test_darktable.py::test_crop_ratio_trims_to_the_ratio",
       "note": "long side of the aspect (5 for 4:5, 3 for 3:2). Negative = crop oriented the other way than the module input (3,-4 is landscape 4:3 on a portrait input); the sign is read from darktable source and from sidecars darktable wrote, a render cannot observe it"}
    ]
